WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.667
PCA.

2
00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:04.730
Dozens of features are impossible to look at.

3
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.800
PCA squeezes them down while keeping what matters.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.067
PCA looks for the directions along which your data varies the most.

5
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:17.013
The first principal component captures the maximum variance.

6
00:00:17.013 --> 00:00:20.233
The second is the best direction perpendicular to it.

7
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:24.267
Mathematically, they are eigenvectors of the covariance matrix.

8
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.933
Here is a cloud of points.

9
00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:30.333
PC1 points along the longest stretch of the cloud.

10
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.454
PC2 is perpendicular to it.

11
00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:36.500
Keep the top ones, drop the rest, and you have a projection.

12
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.433
How much information survives?

13
00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:42.171
The explained variance ratio tells you.

14
00:00:42.171 --> 00:00:49.233
In this example, the first two components keep forty six and twenty one percent, so sixty seven percent in total.

15
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:52.667
In scikit-learn it takes a few lines.

16
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:56.367
We standardize first, so features have comparable scales.

17
00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.533
Then we keep two components and transform the data.

18
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:03.133
The ratio tells us how much of the story the plot shows.

19
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:06.833
A limit to remember: PCA is linear.

20
00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.273
It can only rotate and project.

21
00:01:09.273 --> 00:01:13.000
Curved structure needs t-SNE or UMAP, which come next.

22
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.533
Here is a real use.

23
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:19.567
Each light curve in the exoplanet pipeline has forty features.

24
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:22.715
Reduce to two dimensions and color by label.

25
00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.600
Confirmed planets form a ridge, while false positives smear.

26
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:34.033
The ratios, zero point three eight and zero point one nine, mean the picture shows fifty seven percent of the story.

27
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:36.096
Let's recap.

28
00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:39.333
PCA finds the directions of maximum variance.

29
00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:42.500
Keep the top few for the best low dimensional shadow.

30
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.767
Standardize first, and remember it is linear only.

31
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.433
Next up: t-SNE.
